    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Main text {.unnumbered}\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "## Sections\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\section{level 1 heading}\n",
        "\\subsection{level 2 heading}\n",
        "\\subsubsection{level 3 heading}\n",
        "\\subsubsubsection{level 4 heading}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Paragraphs\n",
        "\n",
        "There is no particular code to write for a paragraph. Just put the text, and put a line break in between paragraphs.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "This is a paragraph.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is another paragraph.\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Lists\n",
        "\n",
        "### Bullet points\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\begin{itemize}\n",
        "  \\item This is the first bullet point\n",
        "  \\item This is the second bullet point\n",
        "  \\item this is the third bullet point\n",
        "\\end{itemize}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Numbered lists\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\begin{enumerate}\n",
        "  \\item This is the first item\n",
        "  \\item This is the second item\n",
        "  \\item this is the third item\n",
        "\\end{enumerate}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Spacing between list items\n",
        "\n",
        "By default there will be a empty line between bullet points. That's usually undesirable unless the bullets contain long multi-line text and spacing them out improves readability. So you will often use **\\\\tightlist** to reduce the space between the items. Like this:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\begin{itemize}\n",
        "  \\tightlist\n",
        "  \\item This is the first bullet point\n",
        "  \\item This is the second bullet point\n",
        "  \\item this is the third bullet point\n",
        "\\end{itemize}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Footnotes\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "This is a text.\\footnote{and this is the footnote for that text.}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Citations\n",
        "\n",
        "At this point we write citations manually, directly in the paragraph so there is nothing specific to do other than making sure they are in proper APA 7 format.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "This is a bit of text in a paragraph (Some author, 2022).\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Quotes\n",
        "\n",
        "Quotes can go straight in the text when less than 40 words or three lines, otherwise use a long quote.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\begin{quote}\n",
        "  This is a quote \n",
        "\\end{quote}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Hyperlinks\n",
        "\n",
        "use the **\\\\url{}**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{latex}\n",
        "\\url{https://www.somewebsite.ca/}\n",
        "```"
      ],
      "id": "9613bbb3"
    }
  ],
